{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548070-any-suggestions-for-stating-samiel","id":1548070,"title":"Any suggestions for stating Samiel?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-30T16:03:05-08:00","id":1548070,"title":"Any suggestions for stating Samiel?","content":"I'm preparing to write a quest (a cyoa style fanfic where you use game mechanics and rolls for those who don't know) where Samiel wakes up in modern nights despite being very dead. From there the game would have a variety of paths open, slaughter the tremere for the death of his sire and murder of his clan, reunite the three castes, purge or take in the warrior antribu, deal with the clans that let the Salubri be butchered, deal with whatever horseshit Saulot is doing, find any allies to help him, try and restore the clan, or try and find Baali to kill, etc. <br /> <br /> But the main issue I am coming across is figuring out what the heck his stats should be. Valeren being nine dots in the warrior path and a few dots in healer are obvious as is high dots in melee and leadership. What's less obvious for me is the rest for him. Any suggestions for what stats would best fit the favorite childe of Saulot?<br /> <br /> Assuming he shouldn't be stat '?' of course. If he is I'd probably just say &quot;Yeah dying took a lot out of you you can't wave your hand and insta gib everyone.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T17:49:32-08:00","id":1548080,"title":"","content":"I think that he should have near max knowledge in occult with a focus on clan history and perhaps infernalism, if your playing a game with others that are playing 4th-6th generation elders and ancients then you should have them with some stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T18:02:06-08:00","id":1548081,"title":"","content":"That makes sense. And would fit him going to war against the Eldest given the giant demon the Eldest made a deal with under those mountains. And the game would be quest, where a group 'plays' a singular character, in this case Samiel so I don't have many stats for other ancients currently.<br /> And when you say near max, you mean 9 dot right? Not five?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-31T03:03:31-08:00","id":1548083,"title":"","content":"In the Clan book it is said Samiel and his warriors trained naked in the wastes of Nod / wastes outside the Second city with the Gangrel and the Brujah <br /> So I would give him a little Celerity and a nice Potance (paired with Fortitude, he went toe to toe with the Eldest and killed him, even if he lost his head after all)<br /> A little Animalism (have a pet wolf or two), Obfuscate (ambush warrior tactics from the Gangrel) or even Protean is not out of the question<br /> A copious amount of Brawl, Survival and Meele is a no brainer<br /> He was always hot headed and ran head first to conflict so probably tactics never were his strong suite, nor sneaking around quietly<br /> But he was a charismatic sonuvabitch and like minded individuals flocked to him, so maybe some Presence or Charisma would played a part or Preformance<br /> I think he would even be a good singer or could play an instrument, flute or lute or lyre... or in modern era a guitar<br /> Originally he was a healer but without Obeah/Healer Valeren, and while not a good one, he did his job, so Medicine and some lore about that age's illneses would linger in his sheet too<br /> <br /> Now According to legend, Samiel received a visitation from Michael, commander of the Heavenly Hosts, while Saulot was away. The archangel directed the warrior king to scribe the Code and to include within it the proper rituals necessary for the strength and blooding of new warriors.<br /> For this I would NOT give him True Faith<br /> Especially becasue he met the Archangle, Faith is... well Faith. At the moment you will know 100% certanity God not only exist but you spoke with an Archangel, it actually kills faith, transform is in to knowledge, at least in my eyes (it is reflected in Demon pretty nicely it is not enough to flash your true form to a mortal, you have to work really hard to lure him in to a Pact and the Pact itself requires the Mortal in question to have faith, preferrably in You)<br /> Samiel is said to have penned this the Code with his own hand but reality it is widely believed he created the Code with the help of his childe Uriel, who is said to have taken dictation about the work from his mighty mentor - so it is possible he not even knew how to write and read, he only spoke Enochian<br /> Again, before the meeting with Mich, she probably not really knew the details, but - especially if you want a nice crossover with Demon: The Fallen and Hunters - the Archangles tutored him about the natrue of Celectials Host and the power of Celestial Names (see the Warrior ability and tradition why they take up the Name of an Angel and able to borrow their power) and the Demons/Fallen Angels, so his occult would be decent enough but maybe not that detailed that one might think<br /> Auspex would be a low one on him (just enough to have the Eye of the Unforgiving Heaven combo discipline), his only precognition was when he knew subconciously he would die and something led him to Qawiyya el-Ghaduba to embrace Her and give her the Code's last complete copy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-31T03:36:54-08:00","id":1548087,"title":"","content":"I like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a>'s profile of him. My only nitpick would be to swap Obfuscate and Protean in favor of Quietus, despite him being more gung-ho than a sneaky assassin type. The Banu Haqim and Salubri were both at the forefront during the Baali Wars, and there is still a lot of mutual respect between the Clans. I would consider it likely that Samiel picked up some of their tricks given their concerted efforts against the Baali. Probably not sorcery though, he doesn't seem the type to me.<br /> <br /> If you want to add a little spice: Daimonion 1 / Sense the Sin. It could represent just a touch of taint he may have acquired during the wars, and being able to see the worst in everyone you meet is a good way to give him some internal conflict and add some depth to his personality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-31T10:53:44-08:00","id":1548096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548070-any-suggestions-for-stating-samiel?p=1548083#post1548083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Clan book it is said Samiel and his warriors trained naked in the wastes of Nod / wastes outside the Second city with the Gangrel and the Brujah<br /> So I would give him a little Celerity and a nice Potance (paired with Fortitude, he went toe to toe with the Eldest and killed him, even if he lost his head after all)<br /> A little Animalism (have a pet wolf or two), Obfuscate (ambush warrior tactics from the Gangrel) or even Protean is not out of the question<br /> A copious amount of Brawl, Survival and Meele is a no brainer<br /> He was always hot headed and ran head first to conflict so probably tactics never were his strong suite, nor sneaking around quietly<br /> But he was a charismatic sonuvabitch and like minded individuals flocked to him, so maybe some Presence or Charisma would played a part or Preformance<br /> I think he would even be a good singer or could play an instrument, flute or lute or lyre... or in modern era a guitar<br /> Originally he was a healer but without Obeah/Healer Valeren, and while not a good one, he did his job, so Medicine and some lore about that age's illneses would linger in his sheet too<br /> <br /> Now According to legend, Samiel received a visitation from Michael, commander of the Heavenly Hosts, while Saulot was away. The archangel directed the warrior king to scribe the Code and to include within it the proper rituals necessary for the strength and blooding of new warriors.<br /> For this I would NOT give him True Faith<br /> Especially becasue he met the Archangle, Faith is... well Faith. At the moment you will know 100% certanity God not only exist but you spoke with an Archangel, it actually kills faith, transform is in to knowledge, at least in my eyes (it is reflected in Demon pretty nicely it is not enough to flash your true form to a mortal, you have to work really hard to lure him in to a Pact and the Pact itself requires the Mortal in question to have faith, preferrably in You)<br /> Samiel is said to have penned this the Code with his own hand but reality it is widely believed he created the Code with the help of his childe Uriel, who is said to have taken dictation about the work from his mighty mentor - so it is possible he not even knew how to write and read, he only spoke Enochian<br /> Again, before the meeting with Mich, she probably not really knew the details, but - especially if you want a nice crossover with Demon: The Fallen and Hunters - the Archangles tutored him about the natrue of Celectials Host and the power of Celestial Names (see the Warrior ability and tradition why they take up the Name of an Angel and able to borrow their power) and the Demons/Fallen Angels, so his occult would be decent enough but maybe not that detailed that one might think<br /> Auspex would be a low one on him (just enough to have the Eye of the Unforgiving Heaven combo discipline), his only precognition was when he knew subconciously he would die and something led him to Qawiyya el-Ghaduba to embrace Her and give her the Code's last complete copy</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much perfect! I agree with the disciplines, they make sense for a warrior trained by Ennoia and Troile. And I agree with no true faith, seeing an actual angel makes it no longer faith, just reality. If Samiel knows angels are on his side then it's not faith it's just logic.<br /> I was thinking a lion for him as a ghouled pet instead of a wolf for animalism. I like the idea of him being a singer of musician, perhaps learning from Rayzeel?<br /> <br /> As for his charisma, I think I prefer the idea of him just being ungodly charismatic, dude got himself put as the main commander of the clans during the Baali wars while not even being the leader of his own clan. I feel like that can't just be presence or Set or Haqim would have overstepped him or ignored the effect when they started directly entering the wars. <br /> <br /> Agree with him not being sneaky. Samiel never met a problem he couldn't solve by stabbing it many times. I really like the idea of him being from a healing clan and being illiterate and having to have relied on medicines to heal instead of Valeren. It gives more depth and a bit of possible insecurity for him.<br /> <br /> I also love the idea of Michael coming down and giving him the downlow on how celestial names worked. Low auspex also makes sense. Though for seeing his future death couldn't that be auspex or the sense the cycle power of the watcher caste?<br /> <br /> (Whatever did happen to Qawiyya anyway? Tremere? Was there a reason she didn't have the name of an angel? DAV20 seems to imply she founded the order of the bitter ashes but that's a one-off line with no other mentions)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548070-any-suggestions-for-stating-samiel?p=1548087#post1548087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a>'s profile of him. My only nitpick would be to swap Obfuscate and Protean in favor of Quietus, despite him being more gung-ho than a sneaky assassin type. The Banu Haqim and Salubri were both at the forefront during the Baali Wars, and there is still a lot of mutual respect between the Clans. I would consider it likely that Samiel picked up some of their tricks given their concerted efforts against the Baali. Probably not sorcery though, he doesn't seem the type to me.<br /> <br /> If you want to add a little spice: Daimonion 1 / Sense the Sin. It could represent just a touch of taint he may have acquired during the wars, and being able to see the worst in everyone you meet is a good way to give him some internal conflict and add some depth to his personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quietus would fit well as a swap out of Obfuscate. And I agree, he is not a sorcerer, mostly because stabbing is more efficient for him.<br /> <br /> The daimonion is perfect! My plan was due to him having multiple accounts of his death, was that when he was betrayed in the baali wars he got his soul eaten by a young Baali... who promptly had his soul beaten bloody and Samiel took over the body due to his mastery of Valeren and it's mastery of the soul, learning Daimonion in the process of taking control. A way to give him a secret shame and temptation of &quot;use the infernal against the infernal.&quot; <br /> <br /> (Speaking of the Baali wars, It's very interesting to me the code forbides working with Setites, yet during the Baali wars he was commanding setites and fighting alongside them.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-02T02:06:14-08:00","id":1548107,"title":"","content":"I figured that you might be going with old school elements and having a Methuselah with 8 or 9 dots would be fitting. But under the current setting it would be a 4 or 5 dot attribute and maybe you should come up with some homebrewed Amalgam powers that would fit the Methuselah's background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-02-2025, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-02T14:36:44-08:00","id":1548116,"title":"","content":"Well, i would do what i always do when in need of a saintly/crusader type of methuselah - purloin <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Michael_(Toreador)#Character_Sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Michael</a>'s stats from Constantinople by Night, max the clan/bloodline favored disciplines, bump some skills a dot up or down according to taste.<br /> <br /> Worked wonders for Cappadocius, goes pretty fine with him too (even though he seems much less prone to religious/martyrdom mania than Capps, Saulot or Michael in his overall portrayal, imho).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-02-2025, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-02T16:27:19-08:00","id":1548118,"title":"","content":"Ask Justin Achilli, he did stat him but never publish them.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-02T16:49:52-08:00","id":1548120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548070-any-suggestions-for-stating-samiel?p=1548116#post1548116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, i would do what i always do when in need of a saintly/crusader type of methuselah - purloin <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Michael_(Toreador)#Character_Sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Michael</a>'s stats from Constantinople by Night, max the clan/bloodline favored disciplines, bump some skills a dot up or down according to taste.<br /> <br /> Worked wonders for Cappadocius, goes pretty fine with him too (even though he seems much less prone to religious/martyrdom mania than Capps, Saulot or Michael in his overall portrayal, imho).</div> </div> </div> </div>Works well! Thank you very much<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548070-any-suggestions-for-stating-samiel?p=1548118#post1548118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ask Justin Achilli, he did stat him but never publish them.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Does he have an account here? Where did he say he stated Samiel, I'd love to read up on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-02T17:21:14-08:00","id":1548122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548070-any-suggestions-for-stating-samiel#post1548070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm preparing to write a quest (a cyoa style fanfic where you use game mechanics and rolls for those who don't know) where Samiel wakes up in modern nights despite being very dead. From there the game would have a variety of paths open, slaughter the tremere for the death of his sire and murder of his clan, reunite the three castes, purge or take in the warrior antribu, deal with the clans that let the Salubri be butchered, deal with whatever horseshit Saulot is doing, find any allies to help him, try and restore the clan, or try and find Baali to kill, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vqgSO8_cRio\" target=\"_blank\">Honestly</a>, if you don't mind me saying <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DSCGoefBO7Q\" target=\"_blank\">it</a>....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548070-any-suggestions-for-stating-samiel?p=1548120#post1548120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Works well! Thank you very much</div> </div> </div> </di